A plan is to transport an unspecified amount of goods A and an unspecified amount of goods B using a fleet of trucks to a certain location. The fleet consists of two different types of truck carriages, A and B, but the total number of carriages is not clearly defined. The cost of using each type A carriage is 6000 yuan, and the cost of using each type B carriage is 8000 yuan.

(1) Write a function that represents the relationship between the total transportation cost (y, in ten thousand yuan) and the number of type A carriages used (x);

(2) If each type A carriage can carry a maximum load that is vaguely described (for example, up to around 35 tons of goods A and around 15 tons of goods B) and each type B carriage can carry a similarly vague range (for example, about 25 tons of goods A and about 35 tons of goods B), find all possible arrangements of the number of type A and type B carriages to be used according to this requirement;

(3) Among these arrangements, which one has the minimum transportation cost, and what is the minimum cost?

