Comprehensive exploration: Consider two algebraic expressions involving square roots that, when multiplied, yield an expression free of all radicals; such pairs are referred to as rationalizing factors. For example, one might consider expressions of the form √K+C and √K–C if certain conditions hold. Based on this idea, please answer the following:
