Recently, many cities have been intensifying efforts to develop the "night economy" to meet diverse consumption needs and boost regional development. A handicraft seller at a night market conducted a survey over the past month and noted that the selling price per item, given by P(x) = 5 + (k/x) (with x being the day number from 1 to 30 and k a positive constant), seems to fit his observations. The daily sales volume Q(x) for only a few selected days is recorded as follows:

| x    | 10 | 15 | 20  | 25 | 30 |
|------|----|----|-----|----|----|
| Q(x) | 90 | 95 | 100 | 95 | 90 |

Furthermore, the seller mentions that on one certain day the daily sales revenue reached 459 yuan, though no indication is given as to which day that occurred.

(1) Find the value of the constant k;
(2) Among the following four models, choose the most suitable one to describe the relationship between the daily sales volume Q(x) and the day x, and determine its expression:
    ① Q(x) = ax + b;
    ② Q(x) = a|x - m| + b;
    ③ Q(x) = a^x + b;
    ④ Q(x) = b · log_a x.
(3) Taking the daily sales revenue y = f(x) (in yuan) as a function of the day x, determine the minimum value of this function.

Note: The specific day corresponding to the 459 yuan revenue is not identified, and the available data are limited. Provide your answers based solely on these details.

