For a function f(x) with domain I, if there exists an interval [m,n] ⊆ I such that f(x) is a monotonic function on the interval [m,n], and the range of the function y=f(x) for x ∈ [m,n] is [m,n], then the interval [m,n] is called a "beautiful interval" of the function f(x);
