In the rectangular coordinate system xOy, with O as the pole and the positive semi-axis of x as the polar axis, the polar coordinate system is established. The polar coordinate equation of the curve C is ρ = 2sinθ + 2a cosθ (a > 0); the parameter equation of the line l is  x = -2 + (√2/2)t,  y = (√2/2)t (t is the parameter), and the line l intersects with the curve C at points M and N.
(1) Write the rectangular coordinate equation of the curve C and the normal equation of the line l;
