In the Cartesian coordinate system xOy, the polar coordinate equation of curve C is \(\rho=4\cos\theta\).  
(1) Find the Cartesian coordinate equation of curve C and the general equation of line n;  
(2) If the x-coordinates of all points on curve C are shortened to \(\frac {1}{2}\) of their original length, and then the resulting curve is translated 1 unit to the left to form curve C1, determine the maximum distance from the points on curve C1 to line n.

Vasya has 9 different books by Arkady and Boris Strugatsky, each containing a single work by the authors. He wishes to arrange these books on a shelf so that two specific pairs of works follow a particular arrangement rule – one rule for the pair including "Beetle in the Anthill" and "Waves Extinguish the Wind", and another, corresponding rule for the pair including "Restlessness" and "A Story About Friendship and Non-friendship". In how many ways can Vasya arrange his books according to these rules?  

Choose the correct answer:  
a) 4 · 7!;  
b) 9!;  
c) 9!/4!;  
d) 4! · 7!;  
e) another answer.

In the polar coordinate system, the curve C₁: ρ = 2cosθ, and the curve C₂: ρsin²θ = 4cosθ. Establish a rectangular coordinate system (xOy) with the pole as the coordinate origin and the polar axis as the positive semi-axis x. The parametric equation of the curve C is { x = 2 + (1/2)t,  y = (√3/2)t } (t is the parameter).
(I) Find the rectangular coordinate equations of C₁ and C₂;
(II) The curve C intersects C₁ and C₂ at four distinct points, arranged in order along C as P, Q, R, and S. Find the value of ||PQ| - |RS||.

Let S = {1,2, …, 15}. From S, extract n subsets A₁, A₂, …, Aₙ, satisfying the following conditions:
(i) |Aᵢ| = 7, for i = 1,2, …, n;
(ii) |Aᵢ ∩ Aⱼ| ≤ 3, for 1 ≤ i < j ≤ n;
(iii) For any 3-element subset M of S, there exists some Aₖ such that M ⊆ Aₖ.

Find the minimum value of n.

A square is inscribed in the ellipse
\[\frac{x^2}{3} + \frac{y^2}{6} = 1,\]so that its sides are parallel to the coordinate axes.  Find the area of the square.

