In the rectangular coordinate system xOy, the ordinary equation of curve C1 is x^2+y^2-2x=0. Establish a polar coordinate system with the origin O as the pole and the positive semi‐axis of x as the polar axis. The polar equation of curve C2 is ρ^2 = 3/(1+2sin^2θ).
(I) Find the parametric equation of C1 and the rectangular equation of C2;
(II) The ray θ=π/3 (ρ≥0) intersects C1 at a point A distinct from the pole, and C2 at point B. Find |AB|.

Calculate the lengths of the arcs of the curves given by the parametric equations.

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \left\{\begin{array}{l}
x=\left(t^{2}-2\right) \sin t+2 t \cos t \\
y=\left(2-t^{2}\right) \cos t+2 t \sin t
\end{array}\right. \\
& 0 \leq t \leq 2 \pi
\end{aligned}
$$

Find the length of side $XY$ in the triangle below.

[asy]
unitsize(1inch);
pair X,Y,Z;
X = (0,0);
Y= (2,0);
Z = (0,sqrt(3));
draw (X--Y--Z--X,linewidth(0.9));
draw(rightanglemark(Y,X,Z,3));
label("$X$",X,S);
label("$Y$",Y,S);
label("$Z$",Z,N);
label("$12$",Z/2,W);
label("$60^\circ$",(1.2,0),N);
[/asy]

Given the ellipse $$C: \frac {x^{2}}{a^{2}}+ \frac {y^{2}}{b^{2}}=1\;(a>b>0)$$ with its left and right foci being F₁ and F₂, and its top vertex being B. If the perimeter of \(\triangle BF₁F₂\) is 6, and the distance from point F₁ to the line BF₂ is \(b\).
(1) Find the equation of ellipse C;
(2) Let A₁ and A₂ be the two endpoints of the major axis of ellipse C, and point P is any point on ellipse C different from A₁ and A₂. The line A₁P intersects the line \(x=m\) at point M. If the circle with MP as its diameter passes through point A₂, find the value of the real number \(m\).

Given the eccentricity \( e= \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \) of an ellipse \( C: \frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}} + \frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}} = 1 \) (with \( a > b > 0 \)) and knowing that one of its focal points lies along the positive x-axis, 
(I) Find the equation of ellipse C;
(II) Let a line through the origin, which is not aligned with any of the coordinate axes, intersect the curve C at two points, M and N, and let A be a point on this line. What is the maximum possible area of the triangle formed by M, A, and N?

Let A = {x | x^2 - ax + a^2 - 19 = 0}, B = {x | x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0}, and C = {x | x^2 + 2x - 8 = 0}.
(1) If A = B, find the value of a;
(2) If B ∩ A ≠ ∅ and C ∩ A = ∅, find the value of a.

Given the ellipse G: x^2/(a^2) + y^2/(b^2) = 1 (a > b > 0) with an eccentricity of (√6)/3, and its right focus at (2√2, 0). A line l with a slope of 1 intersects the ellipse G at points A and B. An isosceles triangle is formed with AB as the base and P (-3, 2) as the apex.

(1) Find the equation of the ellipse G;

(2) Calculate the area of △PAB.

