In ΔABC, a, b, c are the sides opposite to angles A, B, C respectively. Given that c = 7/2, the area of ΔABC is 3√3/2, and tan A + tan B = √3 (tan A tanB - 2),

(1) Find the measure of angle C;

(2) Find the value of a+b.

