The famous German mathematician Dirichlet made significant achievements in the field of mathematics. He was the first person in the history of mathematics to pay attention to concepts and consciously "replace intuition with concepts." The function named after him, D(x) = { 1, x is rational; 0, x is irrational }, is called the Dirichlet function. Now, a function similar to the Dirichlet function is defined as L(x) = { x, x is rational; 0, x is irrational }. There are four conclusions about the Dirichlet function and the L function:
