\( p(x, y, z) \) is a polynomial with real coefficients such that:
1. \( p(tx, ty, tz) = t^2 f(y - x, z - x) \) for all real \( x, y, z, t \) (with some function \( f \));
2. \( p(1, 0, 0) = 4 \), \( p(0, 1, 0) = 5 \), and \( p(0, 0, 1) = 6 \);
3. \( p(\alpha, \beta, \gamma) = 0 \) for some complex numbers \( \alpha, \beta, \gamma \).

Find \( |\gamma - \alpha| \).

