In the Cartesian coordinate system (xOy), the parametric equations of curve C₁ are given by x = 2t - 1, y = -4t - 2 (t is the parameter), and in the polar coordinate system with the coordinate origin O as the pole and the positive half of the x-axis as the polar axis, the polar equation of curve C₂ is ρ = 2/(1 - cos θ).

(1) Write the Cartesian equation of curve C₂;

(2) Let M₁ be a point on curve C₁, and M₂ be a point on curve C₂. Find the minimum value of |M₁M₂|.

