Note that when we say the grid is 5 by 5 we mean that each row and column contains 5 dots!

There are 1000 toy bears in a row. The bears come in three colors: white, brown, and black. Among any three consecutive bears, there is at least one bear of each color. Iskander tries to guess the colors of the bears. He made five guesses:

- The 2nd bear from the left is white;
- The 20th bear from the left is brown;
- The 400th bear from the left is black;
- The 600th bear from the left is brown;
- The 800th bear from the left is white.

It turns out that exactly one of his guesses is wrong. What could be the number of the bear whose color Iskander did NOT guess correctly? Select all possible answers.

Given an ellipse C: x^2/a^2 + y^2/b^2 = 1 (a > b > 0) with an eccentricity of 1/2, a circle with the origin as its center and the short axis of the ellipse as its radius is tangent to the line √7 x − √5 y + 12 = 0.
(1) Find the equation of the ellipse C;
(2) Let A(–4, 0), and a line l passing through point R(3, 0) intersecting the ellipse C at points P and Q. Connect AP and AQ intersecting the line x = 16/3 at points M and N, respectively. If the slopes of lines MR and NR are k₁ and k₂, respectively, determine whether k₁k₂ is a constant value. If it is, find this value; otherwise, explain the reason.

Given the function f(x)=x^3+ax^2+x+1 which achieves an extremum at x=-1 where the tangent line is vertical, find:
(1) the equation of the tangent line to f(x) at (0, f(0));
(2) the maximum and minimum values of f(x) on the interval [-2, 0].

Given the function f(x)=2√3 sin²x - sin(2x - c), where c is a nonzero constant,
(Ⅰ) Find the smallest positive period of f(x) and describe the intervals on which f(x) is monotonically increasing;
(Ⅱ) Suppose that for some α ∈ (0, π) we have f(α/2)=1/2+√3, determine the value of sinα;
(Ⅲ) If x ∈ [-π/2, 0], find the maximum value of f(x).

