Given \(\overrightarrow{m} = (\sin \omega x + \cos \omega x, \sqrt{3} \cos \omega x)\) and \(\overrightarrow{n} = (\cos \omega x - \sin \omega x, 2\sin \omega x)\) with \(\omega>0\), consider the function \(f(x) = \overrightarrow{m} \cdot \overrightarrow{n}\). Assume that the separation between two consecutive symmetry axes of \(f(x)\) is at least a certain positive constant. 
