In the rectangular coordinate system (xOy), consider the curve C₁ defined by { x = a cos φ, y = b sin φ } with the condition a > b > 0, and in the polar coordinate system (with O as the pole and the positive x-axis as the polar axis) consider the curve C₂: ρ = 2 cos θ. A ray l, with equation θ = α (ρ ≥ 0), intersects C₁ at a point P. Assume that for one value of α the ray l meets C₂ at two points with a distance between them equal to a certain fixed number, and that for another value of α the ray meets C₂ so that the distance from O to P equals another fixed number. 
