Since 2021, the "Study Strong Country" app has launched a "Four-Person Match" answer module. The rules are as follows: Users need to answer two rounds of questions in this match. At the beginning of each round, the system automatically matches 3 people to answer questions with the user, and at the end each round, the participants are ranked based on their performance. However, only the probabilities related to ranking in the rounds are provided: the user has an equal chance of ranking first, second, third, or fourth in the first round; moreover, if the user ranks first in the first round, the chance of ranking first in the second round is 1/5, while if not, the chance of ranking first in the second round is 1/3. The scores corresponding to each rank in either round are not specified. 

