(2) If a, b, and c form an arithmetic sequence with a positive common difference, find the value of cos A - cos C.

Given the function f(x)=ax^3 - 4x + 4, where a∈ℝ and f′(x) is the derivative of f(x), and knowing that f′(1) is a negative number, answer the following:

(1) Determine the value of a;

(2) Determine the extreme values of the function f(x).

