In the Cartesian coordinate system xOy, point F is a focus of the ellipse C: (x^2)/(a^2) + (y^2)/(b^2) = 1 (a > b > 0), and point B1(0, -√3) is a vertex of C, ∠OFB1 = π/3.

(1) Find the standard equation of C;

(2) If point M(x₀, y₀) is on C, then point N(x₀/a, y₀/b) is called an "ellipse point" of point M. The line l: y = kx + m intersects C at points A and B, and the "ellipse points" of A and B are P and Q respectively. If the circle with diameter PQ passes through point O, find the area of △AOB.

A grid consists of multiple squares, as shown below. Count the different squares possible using the lines in the grid.

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);
int i, j;
for(i = 0; i <= 5; ++i) {
    draw((0,i)--(5,i));
    draw((i,0)--(i,5));
}
for(i = 1; i <= 4; ++i) {
    for (j = 1; j <= 4; ++j) {
        if ((i > 1 && i < 4) || (j > 1 && j < 4)) continue;
