Given the ellipse C₁: x²/8 + y²/4 = 1 with left and right foci F₁ and F₂, a line l₁ is drawn through point F₁ perpendicular to the x-axis. Line l₂ is perpendicular to l₁ at point P, and the perpendicular bisector of segment PF₂ intersects l₂ at point M.

(I) Find the equation of the trajectory C₂ of point M;
(II) Two perpendicular lines AC and BD are drawn through point F₂, intersecting ellipse C₁ at points A, C and B, D respectively. Find the minimum value of the area of quadrilateral ABCD.

