Given a parabola C: y^2 = 2px (p > 0) and a circle M: (x-2)^2 + y^2 = 4, point P(x0, y0) (x0 ≥ 5) is a point on the parabola in the first quadrant. Through point P, two tangent lines to circle M are drawn, intersecting the x-axis at points A and B.

(1) Find the equation of the parabola C;
(2) Find the minimum value of the area of △PAB.

