A certain township responded to the call of "green waters and green mountains are mountains of gold and silver" and tailored the town to be a "ecological fruit characteristic town" according to local conditions. After investigation, it was found that the yield W (unit: kg) of a certain fruit tree is related to the amount of fertilizer x (unit: kg) applied as follows: W(x)= {5(x^2+3), 0≤x≤2; (50x)/(1+x), 2＜x≤5}. The cost of fertilizer input is 10x yuan, and other cost inputs (such as cultivation management, fertilization, and labor costs) are 20x yuan. It is known that the market price of this fruit is approximately 15 yuan/kg, and the sales are smooth and in short supply. Let the profit per tree of this fruit be f(x) (unit: yuan).
(1) Find the relationship formula of the profit per tree f(x) (yuan) with respect to the amount of fertilizer applied x (kg);
(2) When the cost of fertilizer input is how much yuan, the maximum profit per tree of this fruit is obtained? What is the maximum profit?

