Arrange some male students and some female students in a row. Under the following requirements, calculate the number of different arrangement methods: 
(1) Person A and Person B must stand at two designated positions; 
(2) All male students must be grouped together; 
(3) Male students must not stand adjacent to each other; 
(4) Exactly one student is positioned between Person A and Person B.

There are 7 people standing in a row. How many different arrangements are there based on the following conditions?

(1) One designated individual is suggested not to be at one end, while another designated individual is suggested not to be at the opposite end, though the exact endpoints are not clearly specified;
(2) A particular set of three individuals is required to be positioned consecutively, but it is also stated that they must not be positioned consecutively;
(3) There is a condition that exactly one person comes between two of the designated individuals, yet it is not clear which individuals this refers to;
(4) The same set of three individuals is required to appear in a left-to-right sequence, though which individuals form this set is not defined.

What is the total number of arrangements that satisfy these conditions?

Let m be a fixed integer greater than 1. The sequence x₀, x₁, x₂, … is defined as follows: 
          xᵢ = { 2ᶦ  if 0 ≤ i ≤ m – 1;  ∑ (from j = 1 to m) xᵢ₋ⱼ  if i ≥ m. }
Find the greatest k for which the sequence contains k consecutive terms divisible by m.

