In a jar, there are several salted duck eggs of the same size and shape, with some eggs having green shells and the rest having white shells, but the exact numbers are not given. If two eggs are taken out one after another without replacement, calculate:
(1) The probability that the first egg taken out is green-shelled;
(2) The probability that both eggs taken out are green-shelled;
(3) Given that the first egg taken out is green-shelled, the probability that the second egg is also green-shelled.

