Given the plane rectangular coordinate system (xOy), with O as the pole and the positive semi-axis of x as the polar axis, establish a polar coordinate system. The polar coordinate equation of the curve C1 is ρ = 4cosθ, and the line l: { x = 1 - (2√5/5)t,  y = 1 + (√5/5)t } (t is a parameter).

