[/asy]

In the Cartesian coordinate system xOy, let F be a focus of the ellipse C defined by (x^2)/(a^2) + (y^2)/(b^2) = 1 (with a > b > 0). Also, suppose that one of the vertices of C is denoted by B1 (its location is not specified), and the angle ∠OFB1 is given to be π/3.

(1) Determine the standard equation of the ellipse C;

(2) For any point M(x₀, y₀) on C, define the corresponding point N = (x₀/a, y₀/b) as its "ellipse point." If a line l: y = kx + m (with unspecified k and m) intersects C at two distinct points A and B, and if the ellipse points of A and B are denoted by P and Q respectively, given that the circle with diameter PQ passes through the origin O, compute the area of △AOB.

Given \(\sin \left( \frac{\pi}{4}-x\right)= \frac{1}{5}\), find the values of the following expressions:

(1) \(\sin \left( \frac{5\pi}{4}-x\right)\);

(2) \(\cos \left( \frac{3\pi}{4}+x\right)\);

(3) \(\sin \left( \frac{\pi}{4}+x\right)\).

Note: No restrictions on \(x\) are provided.

Given an arithmetic sequence {aₙ} with the sum of the first n terms Sₙ, and a₁, a₄, a₁₃ form a geometric sequence.
(1) Find the general formula for the sequence {aₙ};
(2) Let {bₙ} be such that the sequence {bₙ/aₙ} is geometric with the first term 1 and a common ratio of 3,
   ① Determine the sum of the first n terms of {bₙ} for any positive integer n;
   ② If the inequality λ·Tₙ - Sₙ + 2n² ≤ 0 holds for all positive integers n, what is the maximum possible value of λ?
Note: Tₙ is defined in a way that depends on additional context.

The red parabola shown is the graph of the equation x = ay^2 + by + c.  Find a+b+c.

[asy]
size(150);
real ticklen=3;
real tickspace=2;

real ticklength=0.1cm;
real axisarrowsize=0.14cm;
pen axispen=black+1.3bp;
real vectorarrowsize=0.2cm;
real tickdown=-0.5;
real tickdownlength=-0.15inch;
real tickdownbase=0.3;
real wholetickdown=tickdown;
void rr_cartesian_axes(real xleft, real xright, real ybottom, real ytop, real xstep=1, real ystep=1, bool

useticks=false, bool complexplane=false, bool usegrid=true) {

import graph;

real i;

if(complexplane) {

label("$\textnormal{Re}$",(xright,0),SE);

label("$\textnormal{Im}$",(0,ytop),NW);

} else {

label("$x$",(xright+0.4,-0.5));

label("$y$",(-0.5,ytop+0.2));

}

ylimits(ybottom,ytop);

xlimits( xleft, xright);

real[] TicksArrx,TicksArry;

for(i=xleft+xstep; i<xright; i+=xstep) {

if(abs(i) >0.1) {

TicksArrx.push(i);

}

}

for(i=ybottom+ystep; i<ytop; i+=ystep) {

if(abs(i) >0.1) {

TicksArry.push(i);

}

}

if(usegrid) {

xaxis(BottomTop(extend=false), Ticks("%", TicksArrx ,pTick=gray

(0.22),extend=true),p=invisible);//,above=true);

yaxis(LeftRight(extend=false),Ticks("%", TicksArry ,pTick=gray(0.22),extend=true),

p=invisible);//,Arrows);

}

if(useticks) {

xequals(0, ymin=ybottom, ymax=ytop, p=axispen, Ticks("%",TicksArry ,

pTick=black+0.8bp,Size=ticklength), above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

yequals(0, xmin=xleft, xmax=xright, p=axispen, Ticks("%",TicksArrx ,

pTick=black+0.8bp,Size=ticklength), above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

} else {

xequals(0, ymin=ybottom, ymax=ytop, p=axispen, above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

yequals(0, xmin=xleft, xmax=xright, p=axispen, above=true, Arrows(size=axisarrowsize));

}
};
real lowerx, upperx, lowery, uppery;
real f(real x) {return -(x+4)*(x+4)/2+5;}
lowery = -9;
uppery = 1;
rr_cartesian_axes(-8,7,lowery,uppery);

draw(reflect((0,0),(1,1))*(graph(f,lowery,uppery,operator ..)), red);

Each tick mark on the graph is one unit.

