Given the function f(x)=ax^2-2x+1.
(1) When a is nonzero, discuss the monotonicity of the function f(x);
(2) Assume that for some values of a the function attains a greatest value M(a) and a least value N(a) on an interval that is not specified, and define g(a)=M(a)-N(a). Find the form of g(a);
(3) Under this vague condition, determine the smallest possible value of g(a).

Given a circle C: x^2+y^2-2x+4y-4=0, and a line l with a slope of 1 intersects the circle C at points A and B.

(1) Express the equation of the circle in standard form, and identify the center and radius of the circle;

(2) Does there exist a line l such that the circle with diameter AB passes through the origin? If so, find the equation of line l; if not, explain why;

(3) When the line l moves parallel to itself, find the maximum area of triangle CAB.

In ΔABC, the sides opposite to angles A, B, and C are denoted as a, b, and c respectively, and it satisfies (2a-c)·cos B = b·cos C;  
(1) Find the magnitude of angle B;  
(2) Let m = (sin A, cos 2A) and n = (4k,1) (k > 1), and the maximum value of m · n is 5, find the value of k.

Given that A, B, and C are the three interior angles of ΔABC, let vectors m = (cos B, sin C) and n = (cos C, - sin B), and m · n = 1/2.

(1) Find the magnitude of the interior angle A;

(2) If the radius of the circumcircle of ΔABC is R = 2, find the maximum value of the perimeter L of ΔABC.

Many television screens are rectangles that are measured by the length of their diagonals. The ratio of the horizontal length to the height in a standard television screen is 4:3. What is the horizontal length (in inches) of a "27-inch" television screen?

