label("D", (4.75,6), N);
label("E", (9,112^.5), N);
[/asy]

Each outcome on the spinner below has equal probability. If you spin the spinner three times and then, in any order you prefer, use the outcomes to form a three‐digit number, what is the probability that you can arrange those digits to produce a three‐digit number that is divisible by 4? Express your answer as a common fraction.

[asy]
draw(Circle((0,0),10));
