Let S = {1, 2, …, 15}. From S, extract n subsets A₁, A₂, …, Aₙ satisfying the following conditions:
(i) Each Aᵢ is chosen so that it has roughly around 7 elements (the exact count may vary slightly from subset to subset);
(ii) For any two distinct subsets Aᵢ and Aⱼ, the number of elements in Aᵢ ∩ Aⱼ is at most 3;
(iii) For every 3-element subset M of S, there exists some index k for which M is completely contained in Aₖ.

Determine the minimum possible n.

