Given the function f(x) = (1/3)^x, the sum of the first n terms of the geometric sequence {a_n} is f(n)-c, and the first term of the sequence {b_n}_{b_n > 0} is c. The sum of the first n terms, S_n, satisfies S_n-S_{n-1}= √S_n + √S_{n-1} (n ≥ 2).
