In the Cartesian coordinate system xOy, the parametric equation of curve C is given by \(\begin{cases} x=3\cos \alpha \\ y=\sin \alpha \end{cases}\) (with \(\alpha\) being the parameter). Also, consider a line l described in a polar coordinate system (with undefined orientation) that is known to intersect curve C at exactly two points.

