(3) The probability that the point (x, y), where x is the number from the first roll and y is the number from the second roll, lies inside the circle defined by x^2+y^2=15.

Due to the increasing personnel exchanges between Hefei and Nanjing, there is a plan to build a dedicated railway that uses a train as a shuttle service. It is stated that the daily round-trip frequency y of the train is a linear function of the number of carriages x it tows each time. In one scenario the train takes a certain number of trips when extra carriages are attached, while in another scenario it makes fewer trips when more carriages are attached.
Ⅰ. Determine the functional relationship between y and x;
Ⅱ. Express the total number S of carriages operated daily as a function of x;
Ⅲ. Assuming each carriage carries 110 passengers, find the number of carriages that should be towed to maximize the daily passenger capacity and state the maximum number of passengers transported.
Note: The specific numerical values relating the number of carriages to the number of daily trips have been omitted.

