Consider an ellipse of the form \(\frac{x^2}{a^2} + \frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1\) \((a > b > 0)\) that has eccentricity \(\frac{\sqrt{6}}{3}\) and suppose that the distance from the origin to the line joining \(A(0,-b)\) and \(B(a,0)\) equals an unspecified constant. 

