A school held a competition on correct eye knowledge as part of its effort to improve children’s eye habits. Some student answer sheets were randomly selected and the scores (x, in points) were recorded, but not all the details were kept. The available information is partly organized into a frequency table with score intervals that cover various ranges, though the exact boundaries for some intervals and the frequency counts are only partially noted. For example, one of the frequency counts is marked by a symbol (a) and several interval limits have been described vaguely. Furthermore, a summary table intended to show overall statistics (like the Mean, Median, and Mode) is provided with one or two of the values obscured. 

