Let A be a set consisting of n elements and let k be a positive integer no larger than n. Determine the maximum possible m for which one may select collections of subsets {B_i} and {C_i} for i = 1, 2, …, m that satisfy all the following: 
(1) Each B_i is a subset of A containing exactly k elements; 
(2) Each C_i is a subset of the corresponding B_i; 
(3) For any two distinct indices i and j, the intersection between B_i and C_j is required to relate to the intersection between B_j and C_i by a rule that is understood in context but not explicitly specified here.
What is the value of m under these conditions?

