In the Cartesian coordinate system xOy, the parametric equations of line l are given by \(x=- \dfrac {\sqrt{3}}{2}t\) and \(y=1+ \dfrac {1}{2}t\), where t is the parameter. A polar coordinate system is established with the origin as the pole and the positive x-axis as the polar axis. Consider a certain curve C₁ (its defining equation is not provided) and let M(6,0) be a fixed point. A point N moves along this curve C₁ and Q is defined as the midpoint of MN.  
(1) Determine the Cartesian coordinate equation of the locus C₂ of point Q;  
