In the rectangular coordinate system (xOy), the curve C₁: { x = a cos φ, y = b sin φ } (with a > b > 0) is given in parameter form, and in the polar coordinate system with O as the pole and the positive x-axis as the polar axis, the curve C₂: ρ = 2 cos θ is given. The ray l: θ = α (with ρ ≥ 0) intersects the curve C₁ at point P, and when α = 0 the ray l intersects the curve C₂ at points O and Q with |PQ| = 1; when α = π/2 the ray l intersects the curve C₂ at point O with |OP| = √3. 
